    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$5.07\u003c/strong\u003e a container (at everyday cost) for a dish restaurants treat as a special occasion. The eggplant is the single biggest line on the list, and it is still a vegetable.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "Eggplant is the biggest line on this list, so buy it in season when the price per each drops. Late summer is when it practically gives itself away in the Midwest.",
                       "The bechamel is butter, flour, milk, an egg, and a little parmesan. That is a small pile of dairy doing the job of a sauce most people think is fancy.",
                       "A gallon of milk costs about the same as a quart-size specialty carton, and you only need a few cups here. Buy the gallon, use the rest for breakfast, and stop paying the small-container tax.",
                       "Parmesan by the tub keeps for months in the fridge and one ounce goes into this whole batch. It is a jar that earns its shelf space across dozens of recipes."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Slice the eggplant into rounds, salt them, and let them sit 20 minutes to draw out water. Pat them dry, brush them with some of the olive oil, and roast at 425F for about 25 minutes until they are soft and browned.",
                    "Peel the potatoes and slice them into thin rounds, brush them with the rest of the olive oil, and roast alongside the eggplant until tender, about 25 minutes. They become the bottom layer that holds the moussaka together.",
                    "While they roast, cook the diced onion in a large pot until soft, add the garlic for a minute, then brown the ground turkey until it reaches 165F.",
                    "Add the tomato sauce, beef broth, cinnamon, oregano, red wine vinegar, bay leaves, salt, and pepper. Simmer 20 minutes until the sauce is thick and almost dry, because a wet meat layer means a soggy casserole.",
                    "Make the bechamel: melt the butter, whisk in the flour and cook two minutes, then pour in the milk slowly while whisking until it thickens. Off the heat, whisk in the beaten eggs, the parmesan, nutmeg, salt, and pepper.",
                    "Layer the roasted potatoes across the bottom of your baking pans, then the eggplant and the meat sauce, pour the bechamel over the top, and smooth it flat.",
                    "Bake at 350F for 45 minutes until the top is set and golden, then let it rest at least 20 minutes so the squares hold together when you cut them.",
                    "Cut the moussaka into 14 even squares and move them into your weighed containers."
                ],
